  "verbalization": "Spiculoic acid A is implicated in the targeting of hepatocytes through multiple pathways, with the drug acting as a target for various compounds that ultimately interact with hepatocytes. The evidence suggests that Spiculoic acid A directly targets the potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which is a key player in cellular ion homeostasis. This subunit is also a target of (2S,3S,4S,5R,6R)-6-[...]-carboxylic acid, a complex molecule that has been shown to interact with hepatocytes. Additionally, Spiculoic acid A is linked to SNU-387, which in turn targets Licochalcone D, another compound that has been identified as a hepatocyte-targeting molecule. The shared involvement of hepatocytes in the targets of these compounds suggests a potential mechanism by which Spiculoic acid A exerts its effects on liver cells. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Spiculoic acid A in modulating cellular processes within hepatocytes, potentially through the regulation of ion transport and other metabolic functions.",
